FIX-03: Close the file descriptor that mkstemp opens

On systems other than Windows, MSXutils_getTempName() makes a temporary
file name with mkstemp(), which also opens the file and returns a
descriptor that was never closed (the file is opened again by name later).
Every MSXopen leaked two descriptors and every MSXsolveH one, so a program
running scenarios one after another in one process ran out of descriptors
after about 80 of them at macOS's default limit of 256 open files.
Close the descriptor. Results are unchanged.

Upstream dev fixed the same leak another way (PR #21), so this patch no
longer applies there.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, on its own:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn FIX-03.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

diff --git a/src/solver/msxutils.c b/src/solver/msxutils.c
index b6caf6b..9a71a56 100644
--- a/src/solver/msxutils.c
+++ b/src/solver/msxutils.c
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@
   #define WINDOWS
 #endif
 
+#ifndef WINDOWS
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
+
 #define UCHAR(x) (((x) >= 'a' && (x) <= 'z') ? ((x)&~32) : (x))
 #define TINY1 1.0e-20
 
@@ -68,8 +72,11 @@ char * MSXutils_getTempName(char *s)
     strcat(s, ptr);
 #else
     // --- use system function mkstemp() to create a temporary file name
+    //     (and close the descriptor it opens; the file is reopened by name)
+    int fd;
     strcpy(s, "msxXXXXXX");
-    mkstemp(s);
+    fd = mkstemp(s);
+    if ( fd >= 0 ) close(fd);
 #endif
     return s;
 }
